## gllvmTMB licensing
##
## gllvmTMB is a standalone Template Model Builder (TMB) package for
## stacked-trait, long-format multivariate generalised linear latent
## variable models (GLLVMs). Except for the components and source lineages
## recorded below, the gllvmTMB-specific code -- including the multi-trait
## engine, formula parser, 5 x 3 covariance keyword grid, response-family
## extensions, diagnostics, and extractors -- is licensed GPL-3 by Shinichi
## Nakagawa.
##
## Family constructors (R/families.R)
##
## The 0.7 family-constructor layer is an independently implemented,
## data-driven gllvmTMB design by Shinichi Nakagawa. It is built from the public
## R family-object contract and `stats::make.link()` semantics. The earlier
## development implementation derived from sdmTMB/glmmTMB family code was
## replaced before the CRAN source freeze; that earlier source is not included
## in the 0.7 tarball. Compatibility is guarded by formals, object-field,
## inverse-link, validation, delta, mixed-family, and compiled-engine tests.
##
## Spatial helper lineage (R/mesh.R, R/crs.R, and R/plot.R)
##
## The original gllvmTMB spatial helper layer was derived from sdmTMB's GPL-3
## implementation. The current helpers were substantially rewritten in place
## against the public fmesher/sf APIs and the published SPDE/GMRF construction.
## gllvmTMB therefore retains conservative sdmTMB attribution rather than
## claiming clean-room authorship. The source baseline is sdmTMB commit
## 8bc452cb743a9efa7b3212653a0f5f2bda3c5ffc (version 0.7.4.9024):
## https://github.com/sdmTMB/sdmTMB/tree/8bc452cb743a9efa7b3212653a0f5f2bda3c5ffc
##
## sdmTMB is GPL-3. Its named authors at that revision include Sean C.
## Anderson, Eric J. Ward, Philina A. English, Lewis A. K. Barnett, and James
## T. Thorson; its complete contributor and copyright-holder roster is retained
## in the pinned DESCRIPTION above. No sdmTMB runtime or build dependency is
## required by gllvmTMB.
##
## TMB engine (src/gllvmTMB.cpp)
##
## Except for the same-author drmTMB helpers recorded below, the C++ template
## under src/gllvmTMB.cpp is original gllvmTMB-native code by Shinichi
## Nakagawa, written against the TMB API (Kristensen et al. 2016,
## https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp). TMB is a runtime dependency (Imports +
## LinkingTo in DESCRIPTION) rather than included source.
##
## The reduced-rank covariance interface and its standard identified
## factor-loading parameterisation were informed by glmmTMB's `rr()` model.
## The current cursor-based lower-triangular unpacker is independently written
## for gllvmTMB; no glmmTMB C++ source is included in this engine.
##
## The stable cumulative-logit helpers `gll_log_inv_logit()`,
## `gll_log1m_inv_logit()`, `gll_log1mexp()`, and
## `gll_log_inv_logit_diff()` are copied verbatim from the sister package
## drmTMB (`src/drm_numeric.h`). Both packages are GPL-3 and both are authored
## by Shinichi Nakagawa; this is same-author GPL-3 reuse.
##
## The broader missing-predictor implementation is also same-author GPL-3
## reuse from drmTMB. It includes the R-side grammar and validators in
## R/missing-predictor.R, the Gaussian/binary/ordered/categorical and grouped
## missing-predictor blocks in src/gllvmTMB.cpp, and their focused tests under
## tests/testthat/test-missing-predictor-*.R. The gllvmTMB code adapts those
## pieces to stacked traits and the package's multi-tier parameter map.
##
## Standalone VA research template (inst/tmb/gllvmTMB_va_r3.cpp)
##
## The standalone variational research template is original gllvmTMB GPL-3
## code by Shinichi Nakagawa. Its dense-tier factor loadings use an
## independently written cursor-based implementation of the same standard
## identified lower-triangular parameterisation; no glmmTMB C++ source is
## included in this template.
##
## Standalone EVA research template (inst/tmb/gllvmTMB_eva.cpp)
##
## The separate extended-variational research template is also original
## gllvmTMB GPL-3 code by Shinichi Nakagawa. Its identified factor loadings are
## unpacked by an independently written cursor traversal; no glmmTMB C++
## source is included in this template.
